@attribute [Route(LegalPages.Terms)]
@attribute [AllowAnonymous]

@* The terms of service the identity server's sign-in page for Beep Oil & Gas links (LegalPages). Public, like the privacy
   policy. Every clause describes how the service actually works: the first account administers and every later one
   starts with no access (RepositoryBootstrapService); access follows roles and asset grants, not the workspace persona;
   records keep who created and changed them; deletion is the account page's, which refuses the only active administrator
   and switches the account off (OilGasAccountDeactivation). The operator is the one TheTechIdea's published legal pages
   name; neither names a registered company, address or governing law, so these terms state none. *@

<PageTitle>Terms of service - Beep Oil &amp; Gas</PageTitle>

<MudContainer MaxWidth="MaxWidth.Medium" Class="py-6">
    <MudPaper Outlined="true" Class="pa-6">
        <MudText Typo="Typo.h4" HtmlTag="h1">Terms of service</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body2" Color="Color.Secondary" Class="mb-4">
            Effective @LegalPages.EffectiveDateText
        </MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-4">
            These terms are the agreement between you and @LegalPages.Operator ("we", "us") for your use of Beep Oil &amp; Gas
            (the "service"). By creating an account or using the service you accept them. If you use the service on behalf of
            an organization, you confirm that you may accept them for it.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Who provides the service</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            Beep Oil &amp; Gas is provided by @LegalPages.Operator. Questions about these terms:
            <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.ContactHref">@LegalPages.ContactEmail</MudLink>.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Your account and your roles</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.VpnKey" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    You sign in through @LegalPages.Operator's identity service,
                    <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.IdentityService" Target="_blank">@LegalPages.IdentityServiceName</MudLink>. Keep
                    your credentials to yourself: anything done through your account is treated as done by you.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.AdminPanelSettings" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    The first person to sign in to the service becomes its administrator. Every account after that starts with
                    no access: an administrator assigns roles, and the fields, wells and other assets each person may reach. What
                    you can see and do follows those roles and grants — the workspace persona you choose only arranges your
                    workspace.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.ManageAccounts" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Administrators are responsible for giving each person only the access they need, and for removing access
                    that people should no longer have.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Block" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    We may suspend or close an account that is used to break these terms, to reach data its holder is not
                    entitled to, or to attack the service.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Acceptable use</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            Do not use the service to break the law; to enter data you have no right to enter, including other people's
            personal data without a lawful reason; to reach records your access does not cover, or to try to get round its
            access controls; to interfere with the service, overload it or test its security without our written permission;
            or to impersonate anyone. We may remove content, or suspend access, that does any of these things.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Your data</MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Inventory" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    The operational, engineering and financial data you and your organization enter remains yours or your
                    organization's. You give us permission to store, process, copy and display it only as needed to provide the
                    service to you and to the people your administrators give access.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.FactCheck" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    You are responsible for having the right to enter what you enter, for its accuracy, and for any personal
                    data it contains — the names and details of lessors, royalty owners, contractors, employees or anyone else.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.History" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Each record keeps who created it and who last changed it. That history is part of the record and stays with it.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Policy" IconColor="Color.Primary">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    How we handle personal data is described in our <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.Privacy">privacy policy</MudLink>.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Calculations, analyses and reports</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-1">
            The service performs engineering and financial calculations — among them decline-curve, nodal, flash, gas-lift,
            choke, compressor, pump, well-test and pipeline analyses, fluid properties, reserves classification, economic
            evaluation, production allocation, royalty, revenue and tax figures, and compliance and emissions reports. They are
            decision support:
        </MudText>
        <MudList T="string" Dense="true" ReadOnly="true" Class="mb-2">
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Calculate" IconColor="Color.Warning">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Their results depend on the data and assumptions entered, and on the limits of the methods used. Check them
                    before you rely on them.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Engineering" IconColor="Color.Warning">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    They are not engineering, geological, reserves, accounting, tax, legal or regulatory advice, and they are not
                    a certification, audit or sign-off by a qualified professional. A reserves classification produced here is
                    not a reserves report or audit, and a compliance, emissions, tax or royalty figure produced here is not a
                    filing.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
            <MudListItem Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Gavel" IconColor="Color.Warning">
                <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
                    Decisions about wells, facilities, safety, spending, reporting and payments remain yours and your
                    organization's, made by people qualified to make them.
                </MudText>
            </MudListItem>
        </MudList>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Availability and changes to the service</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            We work to keep the service available, but we do not guarantee uninterrupted service: maintenance, hosting failures
            and outages at the identity service or other services it depends on all happen. We may change, add or remove
            features. Keep your own copies of anything you cannot afford to lose, and do not rely on the service as the only
            record of something that matters to you.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Ending your use</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            You may stop using the service at any time. You can delete your account from the Personal Data tab of
            <MudLink Href="@BeepClientEndpoints.Manage">your account page</MudLink>: that deletes your sign-in account at the
            identity service and switches your Beep Oil &amp; Gas account off. If you are the only active administrator, make
            someone else an administrator first. The records you created stay, as part of your organization's history; the
            <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.Privacy">privacy policy</MudLink> explains what remains and how to ask about it. We may
            suspend or close an account as described above, proportionately, and with a warning first where the circumstances
            allow one.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Disclaimer and limitation of liability</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            The service is provided as it is. To the fullest extent the law allows, we exclude implied warranties, and we are
            not liable for indirect or consequential loss, for loss of data, profit, production or opportunity, or for
            decisions made on the strength of the service's calculations, analyses or reports. Nothing in these terms limits
            liability that cannot lawfully be limited — including for death or personal injury caused by negligence, or for
            fraud.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Changes to these terms</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1" Class="mb-2">
            We may update these terms as the service changes. The date at the top is when this version took effect, and
            continuing to use the service after a change means the updated terms apply.
        </MudText>

        <MudText Typo="Typo.h6" HtmlTag="h2" Class="mt-6 mb-2">Contact</MudText>
        <MudText Typo="Typo.body1">
            Questions about these terms: <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.ContactHref">@LegalPages.ContactEmail</MudLink>. How we
            handle your data is described in our <MudLink Href="@LegalPages.Privacy">privacy policy</MudLink>.
        </MudText>
    </MudPaper>
</MudContainer>
